      <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">VIEW FROM THE CHAIR'S DESK</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 11pt;">It is becoming increasingly clear, as I conclude my first term as department chair and embark on my second, that I have the privilege of leading a department in the midst of such a dynamic change in the arrival in 2014 of Ens Dwyer and Shesko as our new trustees. History is one of the U.S. Civil War era and Latin America, respectively—added to the department created by the recent hires of Yan Li in Chinese history and James Naus as our Medievist. Collectively, these four outstanding scholars and teachers bring the department a vital infusion of enthusiasm, dynamism, and talent. Not only have they helped to shift the department's center of balance in a new direction, they will also help substantially shape our college and department in the coming years. I am excited about the future of our department and the new colleagues who have joined us. I look forward to continuing to work with all of you.</p>
    </div>
