      <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">STUDENT SCHOLARSHIP WINNERS ANNOUNCED</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 11pt;">History majors Sarah Black and Adam Denton have been recognized for their outstanding achievements by being named recipients of two prestigious scholarships for the upcoming 2015-16 academic year. Sarah Black has been named a recipient of the History Scholarship awarded by the Department of History for 2015-16. Congratulations to Sarah and Adam on these honors.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Graduate student Katie Chaka, who will be the department's graduate assistant, starting in the fall, won a competitive research award in the field of American History, which is much as she conducts research on her M.A. thesis.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Additionally, thanks to the work of Professor Erin Dwyer, the Dean's office has funded a new summer research fellowship for the History Department. This fellowship is a competitive application process to support graduate students. Congratulations to <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span>, <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span>, <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span>, and <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span> for their accomplishments.</p>
